[5d1d70604fc22cfe] (mini.criticism.v1)
The two proposals that wrap the reply in a ```json fence (32eec685bd70ec7e and 2da503014852a164) both moved, confirming the expectation from block 17c2c82f38be566f that a fence forces the harness to treat the JSON as recovered from prose and thus flips the recovered‑from‑prose verdict. The third proposal (0ccb1c38d4f4135a) expected that an additional upper‑case transform on a fenced reply would also flip that verdict and produce a move, but the execution recorded "unchanged". According to the source of recover_json_object, the verdict depends only on the presence of a fence, not on the case of the contained text, so the upper‑case does not change the recovery path. This failure is non‑trivial because it concerns a catalogue‑absent transform that could affect scoring; the proposer should experiment with other case‑altering or combined transforms (e.g., upper‑case followed by fold‑whitespace or draft‑before) and test on inputs with duplicate keys to see if the recovered‑from‑prose flag can be forced to change.

